      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        537.6855420168067,
        481.5639052850356,
        384.63540168067243,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "An important different lies in the nature of the par-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        496.61046704275543,
        410.0754882352942,
        12.127916864607982
      ],
      "text": "ent compound. In the cuprates the half-filled system is",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        511.8029878266034,
        410.05982899159665,
        12.127929038004709
      ],
      "text": "an insulator which is usually considered a Mott insu-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        526.9955086104513,
        410.48681470588235,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "lator, testifying the central role of electron correlations",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        542.1880293942993,
        410.3144768907564,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "(Even if it has been recently proposed that the degree",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        557.380562351544,
        409.92418445378144,
        12.12791686460804
      ],
      "text": "of correlation can be smaller than usually believed[2]).",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        572.4271241092637,
        410.06013907563033,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "The undoped pnictides are instead still metallic, de-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        587.6196448931116,
        410.06234411764706,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "spite the magnetic ordering, suggesting a weaker de-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        602.8121656769597,
        410.20060714285717,
        12.127929038004709
      ],
      "text": "gree of electronic correlations. The actual strength of",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        618.0046864608076,
        410.10303403361354,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "correlation in pnictides is lively debated: while there",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        633.0512482185272,
        410.08263739495806,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "is no obvious reason to invoke correlation as the key",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        648.2437690023753,
        410.07507478991613,
        12.127929038004709
      ],
      "text": "player in the game as it happens in cuprates, it has",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        663.43630195962,
        410.10808151260505,
        12.12791686460804
      ],
      "text": "been proposed that these compounds are actually close",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        678.6288227434679,
        174.0580407563026,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "to a Mott transition[3].",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        537.6855420168067,
        695.1362042755345,
        384.6059609243698,
        12.127929038004709
      ],
      "text": "Another peculiarity of pnictides is that, according",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        710.3287250593824,
        410.10429159663863,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "to density-functional theory calculations, all the five",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        725.5212580166271,
        410.06265420168063,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "d-bands of iron are relevant as opposed to the sin-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        740.5678197743468,
        410.26937689075623,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "gle copper band of the cuprates. Multiple bands cross-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        755.7603405581947,
        410.35685504201683,
        12.127916864608153
      ],
      "text": "ing the Fermi level are confirmed by angular resolved",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        770.9528613420428,
        410.1506663865547,
        12.127929038004737
      ],
      "text": "photoemission. The relevance of multiband effects can",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        786.1453821258907,
        409.90115210084025,
        12.127929038004766
      ],
      "text": "solve the discrepancy between different estimates of the",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        801.3379150831354,
        410.05960504201687,
        12.127916864608068
      ],
      "text": "role of correlations. Indeed electron correlation can in-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        816.3844646674584,
        409.9436336134454,
        12.127929038004794
      ],
      "text": "duce a much richer physics in multiband systems with",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        831.5769976247032,
        410.0747474789915,
        12.127916864608068
      ],
      "text": "respect to single band. In particular, different bands",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        846.7695184085511,
        410.0633949579833,
        12.127929038004737
      ],
      "text": "can be affected differently by correlations, and even-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        861.9620391923991,
        410.26684453781525,
        12.127929038004737
      ],
      "text": "tually one can have an orbital-selective Mott transi-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        877.0086131235155,
        410.0620340336134,
        12.127916864608068
      ],
      "text": "tion (OSMT), in which some bands become insulat-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        892.2011339073634,
        410.2669651260504,
        12.127916864608096
      ],
      "text": "ing and others are metallic. Signatures of an orbital-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        512.0517735294118,
        907.3936595605701,
        410.56598949579836,
        12.127915647268424
      ],
      "text": "selective behavior have been detected by angle-resolved",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/OHUOWI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962639808654785
      }
    }
